    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "wallet: fail importdescriptors when shutdown interrupts rescan",
    "user": {
      "login": "Turtlecute33",
      "id": 95269376,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBa2yAA",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95269376?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Turtlecute33",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Turtlecute33/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "**Problem:** If the node is stopped while `importdescriptors` is rescanning, the call still returns success for descriptors whose history was not scanned. The wallet's best block is already at the tip, so nothing rescans on the next start, and the transactions stay missing until a manual `rescanblockchain`.\n\n**Fix:** Treat a rescan that shutdown cut short like one stopped with `abortrescan`: the import fails with the existing \"Rescan aborted by user.\" error. In both cases the descriptors stay in the wallet.\n",
